		{
			"id": "112683907839601132",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://ruby.social/@konnorrogers/112683907779949255",
			"author": {
				"name": "Konnor Rogers",
				"url": "https://ruby.social/@konnorrogers",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/326/194/727/800/237/original/c5edef7eca753a07.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2024-06-26T16:39:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> You're onto something here.Also packages that explicitly require bundlers.</p><p>I promise I'm not here to air more small dev grievances, but on a sister repository I was told that the proper way to ship libraries is untranspiled CJS.</p><p>Which gets back to your point of \"is this package intended to run in a browser\" and \"can this run without a compilation step or Node polyfills etc\"</p><p>(For reference)</p><p><a href=\"https://github.com/A11yance/aria-query/pull/485\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/A11yance/aria-query</span><span class=\"invisible\">/pull/485</span></a></p><p>NPM needs some tags!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112683914758977740",
			"parentId": "112683907839601132",
			"url": "https://ruby.social/@konnorrogers/112683914720518531",
			"author": {
				"name": "Konnor Rogers",
				"url": "https://ruby.social/@konnorrogers",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/326/194/727/800/237/original/c5edef7eca753a07.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2024-06-26T16:41:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The other problem when you \"make these agreements\", is usually someone else has also made the agreement for you, making it even harder to track down.</p><p>In the \"aria-query\" example, its a dependency of dom-testing-library, and I hit the issue while using react-testing-library, which relies on dom-testing-library, which relies on aria-query</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
