				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/315/100/329/990/772/original/74ebe12d2f7e951a.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-06-27T08:36:03.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> this has been soo weird to me, and *particularly* since Wasm came about and people started compiling JS engines to Wasm (for small embedded scripting systems &amp; for sandboxing). While \"systems\" languages like Rust has a notion of std/nostd to cater for embedded &amp; Wasm and a ton of other usecases the best we got is WinterCG but otherwise the JS ecosystem likes to pretend every script still runs in Netscape Navigator 4.0 and there aren't like 796 different embeddings of V8 and a 100 other JS engines and runtimes in mobile apps, the cloud, the edge, in space suits and bloated desktop apps...</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
